00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:18.200
names fills at the opening print but the actual mechanism driving that price is the market repricing

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:25.880
the probability of a bank of Canada pause versus cut. The bid asks spread on sector ETFs can widen from

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:33.120
3 cents to 12 cents in the first 15 minutes after the 8.30am release as dealers hedge delta exposure.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:39.540
What most retail investors don't realize is that the inflation number itself does not move prices.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:45.540
The surprise relative to consensus does and that surprise is already partially reflected

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:52.720
in futures markets by 8.29am. The biggest mistake with inflation day rebalancing is treating the data

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:59.600
release as a binary buy or sell signal. Instead always wait for the 20-minute volume weighted average

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:05.600
price after the print before executing the rotation. Given today's lack of clean setups,

